\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces DAO improves with training budget on 105 held-out adapters and has not saturated. Exact match rises from 3/105 at 6 epochs to 36/105 at 12 and 58/105 at 25, with 95\% Wilson intervals; nearest-neighbor retrieval over the same tokens reaches 13.3\%, and the matched shuffled-token control stays at zero throughout. Chance is $1/155$. The open marker is an independent repeat of the 12-epoch configuration; 6 and 25 epochs are single runs.}}{5}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:epochs}{{3}{5}{DAO improves with training budget on 105 held-out adapters and has not saturated. Exact match rises from 3/105 at 6 epochs to 36/105 at 12 and 58/105 at 25, with 95\% Wilson intervals; nearest-neighbor retrieval over the same tokens reaches 13.3\%, and the matched shuffled-token control stays at zero throughout. Chance is $1/155$. The open marker is an independent repeat of the 12-epoch configuration; 6 and 25 epochs are single runs}{figure.3}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Held-out-adapter performance. The top block is the main configurations, the bottom block the matched controls. Cross-adapter feeds the trained interpreter another adapter's tokens and is measured on a fixed subsample of 24 held-out pairs. Normalized retrieval rank is 0.5 at chance. Arrows give the direction of better. Chance exact-match accuracy is 0.0065.}}{5}{table.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:main}{{1}{5}{Held-out-adapter performance. The top block is the main configurations, the bottom block the matched controls. Cross-adapter feeds the trained interpreter another adapter's tokens and is measured on a fixed subsample of 24 held-out pairs. Normalized retrieval rank is 0.5 at chance. Arrows give the direction of better. Chance exact-match accuracy is 0.0065}{table.1}{}}
